    "text": "Is the uniform subgroup membership problem decidable for (finitely generated\nfree)-by-cyclic groups? That is, for a fixed group G = Fn ⋊ Z, is there an algorithm\nthat, given elements w, h1 , . . . , hk ∈ G, decides whether or not w belongs to the\nsubgroup H = ⟨h1 , . . . , hk ⟩?                                          I. Kapovich",
